{"id": "EUVD-2026-82141", "enisaUuid": "894db01a-645e-3c53-b3f8-08abc62079bf", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nbpf: Zero queue and stack outputs on lock failure\n\nQueue and stack pop/peek helpers accept an uninitialized output buffer\nbecause the verifier expects the helper to initialize it. The empty-map\nerror path clears the buffer, but a failed lock acquisition returns\n-EBUSY without writing it.\n\nClear the output before returning -EBUSY so BPF programs cannot observe\nuninitialized stack contents after a failed helper call.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:10:27", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:51:46", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a6090eeb289c5fa45f7b629befac2bd3c19a6dae", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/23b4bcc79bab5285275912b94e98c286f281de75", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1534c4bff3aaca19c4c9a82f93e9b81f7c983de3", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e2396b8a562073787e627a5f483f1bc5c452fa6a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7ac6e1ae41a09f1dd4baeeff1d028ae49ee01232"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-92520", "GHSA-fc4c-4457-gw27"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0d4a08e7-695b-32bd-a508-bf5ab1f72185", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "388c9d3eefaea99828ee5000c693128a5b41ee7c"}, {"id": "17ea6450-9216-3729-95e9-828a99ac9ee7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "232f0ba4d69263af5912e279fcc32fef2882b1dc"}, {"id": "2871358f-6cfe-3cf3-ba5a-781d8efd9a96", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e388671635acf470f0986d874389148fd234620b"}, {"id": "3f4d81ca-c552-325b-bea8-371ca031c939", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.1.56 <6.2"}, {"id": "4ddacb23-e2bd-3a97-9a20-5d5b0418c01c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "6804ec